Same defect as cpp11_alias_template_short_name_capture but with a
COMPLETED class (not the in-progress one) as the same-short-named
argument, and the alias chain used directly at function scope: the
member alias's `_If<_Bp, ...>` must resolve to the namespace-scope
alias template, not to __conditional_t's `_If` type parameter's
binding `S`.
